{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-89047-r4615143","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Borhani (Spiced Yogurt Drink)","sourcePageId":89047,"sourceRevision":"4615143","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-02-03T02:24:47Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Borhani%20(Spiced%20Yogurt%20Drink)&oldid=4615143","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:24:45.135Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Easy recipes","Category:Indian recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for beverages","Category:Recipes using chile","Category:Recipes using coriander","Category:Recipes using mint","Category:Recipes using mustard seed","Category:Recipes using sugar","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Vegetarian recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"8aff85284ec52c3dc4bfa43842a80def30245f17c3e40a6b5304922addbd7f5b","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Beverage recipes\n| Servings = 6\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Beverages|Beverages]] | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of India|Indian Cuisine]]\n\n'''Borhani''' are [[Cookbook:Yogurt|yoghurt]]-based drinks popular in Bangladesh. It's traditionally served in wedding ceremonies around the country.\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Cumin|cumin]] seeds\n* 500 [[Cookbook:mL|mL]] (2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]]) full-fat plain [[Cookbook:Yoghurt|yoghurt]]\n* 1 cup (200 [[Cookbook:mL|mL]]) cold water\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] fresh green [[Cookbook:Chiles|chile peppers]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Mint|mint]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Coriander|coriander]]\n* ¾ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Mustard|white mustard seeds]]\n* ¾ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Pepper|ground white pepper]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Black Pepper|ground black pepper]]\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Salt|rock salt]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# Dry-[[Cookbook:Roasting|roast]] cumin seeds by cooking them over low heat in small [[Cookbook:Frying Pan|pan]] until you can smell the seasoning, about 2 minutes. Cool and grind to a powder.\n# Beat yoghurt with water until it becomes smooth. Strain green chili, mint, leaf and coriander pastes with some water blend into the yoghurt. Combine all other ingredients and mix well.\n# Serve cold.\n\n[[Category:Indian recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mint]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using coriander]]\n[[Category:Recipes for beverages]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mustard seed]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Borhani (Spiced Yogurt Drink)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"6","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"3 tsp cumin seeds","sourceText":"3 tsp cumin seeds","amountText":"3 tsp cumin seeds","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"500 mL (2 cups) full-fat plain yoghurt","sourceText":"500 mL (2 cups) full-fat plain yoghurt","amou